  "notes": "FORMATION: Compound of {身|み} (body) + {悶|もだ}える (to writhe). The prefix {身|み} emphasizes the involvement of the whole body.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}).\n\nCONJUGATION: Ichidan verb: {身悶|みもだ}えない, {身悶|みもだ}えます, {身悶|みもだ}えて.\n\nUSAGE: Often used figuratively for emotional distress (embarrassment, frustration) where one metaphorically wants to writhe.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}み/{苦|くる}しみに{身悶|みもだ}える (to writhe in pain/agony)\n- {恥|は}ずかしさに{身悶|みもだ}える (to squirm with embarrassment)\n- {身悶|みもだ}えするほど (to the point of writhing)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {悶|もだ}える (to writhe - less emphatic)\n- のたうち{回|まわ}る (to roll around in agony)\n- {身|み}をよじる (to twist one's body)",
